{
  "title": "Trace-only catalog entries for spices with no citable calories",
  "description": "The 2026-10-01 classification pass (FNDDS plus cited USDA Branded labels) skipped 94 names (420 corpus lines, 102 prod lines) whose only Branded labels use servings under 10 g, which round to 0 kcal and can't be cited: celery salt, sumac, Cajun and Old Bay seasoning, Aleppo pepper, za'atar, five spice, asafoetida, MSG, dashi granules, bonito flakes, liquid smoke. \
They stay Unresolved, so even 'a pinch of sumac' or 'celery salt to taste' counts as an unknown line. \
Proposal: let a curated entry be trace-only, {\"trace_ok\": true} with no fdc_id and no calories (the loader already accepts it). \
Such a line is negligible when it has no amount, a trace unit, or at most a tablespoon (the existing spoonful rule for foods with no density), and unknown for any larger amount. \
Add an apply-script action for it, classify the spice-like names from logs/catalog-classification-2026-10-01.json skips (not sauces or pastes such as tonkatsu sauce or harissa), and re-audit prod.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 2,
